Proposed Hardware

MCU and radio: nRF54L15, one per unit
(https://docs.nordicsemi.com/r/bundle/ps_nrf54l15/page/keyfeatures_html5.html)

Audio codec: TLV320AIC3204, one per unit; ADC on transmitter and DAC/headphone drivers on receiver
(https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tac5112.pdf)

Oscillator: SiT8008BC-22-33E-12.288000G, one per unit
(https://www.mouser.com/datasheet/3/708/1/SiT8008B_datasheet.pdf)

Debugger: NRF54L15-DK + 1.27 mm Cortex SWD ribbon cable (order through maker club)
(https://www.digikey.com/en/products/detail/nordic-semiconductor-asa/NRF54L15-DK/25601516) + (https://www.amazon.com/dp/B01D0YSTBE?lv=shuf&channelId=500&plpRedirect=mhFallback)

Guitar interface: Additional low-noise high-impedance input buffer on transmitter

Clocking: Compatible codec/I2S audio clocks plus firmware correction for transmitter/receiver clock drift

Antenna: Custom 2.4 GHz PCB antenna on each unit

RF circuitry: Nordic package-specific reference matching/filter network, 50-ohm PCB transmission line, and separate antenna tuning footprints

RF test connection: Selectable SMA connection for comparing the custom PCB antenna with an external antenna

Antenna placement: PCB edge with geometry-specific clearance; tune and test with enclosure, battery, headphone cable, and body nearby

Power circuitry: Regulators and decoupling; battery protection and charging for portable version

Debug access: SWD programming connector and power, clock, I2S, and control test points


Signal Path

Transmitter: Guitar -> input buffer/conditioning -> codec ADC -> nRF54L15 -> RF matching/filter -> transmission line -> antenna tuning -> custom PCB antenna
Receiver: Custom PCB antenna -> antenna tuning -> transmission line -> RF matching/filter -> nRF54L15 -> codec DAC/headphone drivers -> headphones

