Connector Wiring:
Receiver SWD programming/debug connector — J1
Debugger: Nordic nRF54L15 DK, P19 DEBUG OUT
Connector: 2×5 male header, 1.27 mm pitch
Cable: matching straight-through ribbon, maximum 10 cm

J1 pin | Signal  | Receiver connection
1      | VTref   | +3V3
2      | SWDIO   | U1 dedicated SWDIO, physical pin 25
3      | SELECT  | GND; selects external target on DK
4      | SWCLK   | U1 dedicated SWDCLK, physical pin 26
5      | GND     | GND
6      | SWO     | Unconnected
7      | NC      | Unconnected
8      | NC      | Unconnected
9      | NC      | Unconnected
10     | nRESET  | U1 dedicated RESET, physical pin 30

SWD uses dedicated chip pins, not the configurable
P1.xx GPIO assignments used for the codec.

Power the receiver separately at 3.3V for debugging.
Pin 1 provides the target voltage reference.

